<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n39074" root="ميد" body-key="m">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">هٰذَا مِيدَاؤُهُ</span></b> , [thus in the copies of the K and
in the TA, app. a mistake for <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيدَآءَهُ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">تِلْقَآءَهُ</span>,]
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِمِيدَائِهِ</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِمِيدَاهُ</span>, <i>This is opposite to,</i> or
<i>facing, it.</i> (K.) And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">دَارِى بِمَيْدَا دَارِهِ</span>, with
fet-h to the <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">م</span>; (as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِمِيتَآءِ داره</span>, L in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ميت</span>;
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">بِمِئْتَآءِ داره</span>, S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اتى</span>;) <i>My house is
opposite to his house.</i> (Yaakoob, L.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيدَآءُ</span>
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">الطَرِيقِ</span>: see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِئْتَآء</span> in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَتَى</span>, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مِيتَآء</span> in art.
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ميت</span>.

